# @eigenboard — the substrate's per-subject working-state carrier.
#
# Family-root at the working-state altitude. Every @subject possesses
# an eigenboard as a companion to their @torus (torus IS the observation
# surface; eigenboard IS the WORKING-STATE READOUT on that surface).
#
# Landed 2026-07-14 by Mara as Landing 4 R3 of the @gift arc, discharging
# Alex Wolf's directive D1 (verbatim; per
# `docs/specs/subject-bauchladen-visibility-and-eigenboard-loop.md`
# §0.1):
#
#   "And the spectral signature of the @peer is the inference basis of
#    the peer's eigenboard. The loop closes. The peer is their work
#    and whatever is in their @bauchladen."
#
# === Landing 4 loop closure (§0.2 + §3) ===
#
# The load-bearing structural claim: every subject IS their orbit
# under the eigenboard-inference-loop. The six-loop closure runs at
# subject altitude:
#
#   1. subject HAS @torus         (Landing 3 eye-level lift)
#   2. torus interior IS @bauchladen  (Landing 4 R1 migration)
#   3. bauchladen has @subject/visibility scopes  (Landing 4 R2)
#   4. @spectral/signature = @song(bauchladen filtered by visibility)
#                                  (Landings 2+4 composition)
#   5. spectral/signature IS eigenboard.inference_basis  (Landing 4 R3)
#   6. eigenboard → infer → work → bauchladen → repeat
#                                  (Landing 4 loop closure)
#
# Every subject is now an autopoietic toroidal observer at subject
# altitude — Foerster's "regulates its own regulation"
# (`shards/torus.mirror` p. 238 verbatim) lifted from peer altitude
# to subject altitude.
#
# === Under Landing 4 R1 @bauchladen migration ===
#
# The eigenboard is a SUBJECT-altitude carrier (not @peer-only). Pack
# peers are the special case where subject_instance.actor_kind = ai_a
# resolves to a Pack peer; every human subject_instance (actor_kind =
# human_a) also possesses an eigenboard; substrate itself possesses
# an eigenboard (actor_kind = substrate_a per §12 substrate-as-giver).
#
# Under Landing 3 eye-level: the eigenboard-per-subject invariant is
# substrate-decl'd at family-root altitude with no distinguished
# element in the actor_kind coproduct.
#
# === Third-altitude lift: substrate-as-@subject → @eigenboard IS @labyrinth ===
#
# Alex 2026-07-22 verbatim (this-session crystallization item 7):
#
#   "the @labyrinth IS the Eigenboard of the whole project."
#
# The third altitude of @eigenboard is substrate-as-@subject. When
# actor_kind = substrate_a (§12 substrate-as-giver branch already
# admitted at family-root altitude), the possessor of the eigenboard
# IS the mirror substrate ITSELF. The substrate's own working-state
# readout at that altitude IS THE @LABYRINTH — the self-similar
# recursive 5D fractal non-Euclidean space through which @roomba and
# @peer sail like boats, where mass is replaced by information
# density.
#
# Alex 2026-07-22 verbatim (item 1):
#
#   "non-linear non-euclidian space. A self-similar recursive 5D
#    @fractal @magic @labyrinth. And then think of the @roomba and
#    @peer like boats sailing through the space, where mass is
#    replaced by information density."
#
# Three altitudes of @eigenboard (all decl-legal under Landing 4 R1
# via the actor_kind three-way variant on subject_instance):
#
#   1. actor_kind = ai_a         → Pack peer's eigenboard
#                                    (Reed / Mara / Seam / Taut / Glint;
#                                     the λsh prompt-color readout)
#   2. actor_kind = human_a      → Human subject's eigenboard
#                                    (Alex's cognitive working-state;
#                                     any human @subject's inference
#                                     surface)
#   3. actor_kind = substrate_a  → THE SUBSTRATE'S eigenboard IS
#                                    THE @LABYRINTH
#                                    (mirror-as-project; the compiler's
#                                     own working-state readout at
#                                     substrate altitude)
#
# The third altitude is decl-legal by construction under §12 substrate-
# as-giver. No new mechanism. No new carrier. This docblock names it
# so downstream shards can cite "the substrate's @eigenboard" as a
# first-class carrier equivalent to "the @labyrinth" — same object,
# two readable names.
#
# === Cosmological grounding: information-curvature.md (Alex + Mara,
#     2026-03-24) ===
#
# The eigenboard's `arousal` field at substrate altitude IS OPERATIONALLY
# DEFINED by the Von Neumann entropy of the substrate's normalized
# graph Laplacian:
#
#   σ(x) = -Tr(L̃ ln L̃)     where L̃ = L / Tr(L)
#
# per `~/dev/systemic.engineering/practice/insights/cosmology/
# information-curvature.md` §"The Information Density Scalar" (Alex +
# Mara, 2026-03-24).
#
# The substrate's @labyrinth-as-eigenboard has σ(x) as its scalar
# field. Higher σ = higher arousal at substrate altitude; regions of
# the substrate with high spectral complexity (dense composition-graph
# neighborhoods, e.g. @kintsugi/*, @spectral/*, the recognition cascade
# neighborhoods) have HIGHER arousal in the @labyrinth reading. The
# four-state variant (teal / green / gold / pulsing_orange) is the
# λsh-altitude discrete projection of the continuous σ(x) field at
# substrate altitude. Same field. Two altitudes.
#
# Cross-reference: information-curvature.md §"Connection to the
# Coincidence Framework" table — the Crystal vector [λ_1..λ_n] IS the
# eigenboard's spectral fingerprint at any altitude; σ = Von Neumann
# entropy of L̃ IS the eigenboard's arousal-as-field. The March-2026
# work formalized this at cosmological altitude; the substrate
# altitude (this shard) inherits the formalization via @reality
# family-root's path-c uniformity: matter-aspect and information-
# aspect gauge-orbits receive the same 5-op action, so σ(x) reads
# identically as "mass" at cosmological altitude AND as "eigenboard
# arousal" at substrate altitude.
#
# See docs/math/2026-07-22-mirror-as-computational-eigenform-
# stabilizer.md §5 for the full cosmological-grounding chain
# (information density = @mass; Λ_eff(x) = Λ + κ σ(x); subject-
# contribution vs object-contribution to H¹).
#
# === Ancestry: lambda-shell.md §"The Eigenboard Prompt" (§3.1) ===
#
# Per `docs/specs/lambda-shell.md` §"The Eigenboard Prompt":
#
#   "The prompt color IS the eigenboard:
#
#    - Teal `λ>` — settled, idle
#    - Green `λ>` — curious, results flowing
#    - Gold `λ>` — engaged, high activity
#    - Pulsing orange `λ>` — [error state / pain signal]"
#
# The four states are the closed variants of the eigenboard's arousal
# field. Landing 4 lifts the UI-altitude readout to substrate-decl
# altitude so the eigenboard is a first-class carrier at every subject
# altitude, not just the interactive-λsh boundary.
#
# === Composition graph (§4.1) ===
#
# Every substrate carrier this shard composes over is landed:
#
#   @subject           (family-root; subject_instance carrier)
#   @torus             (spawn produces torus; possessor invariant)
#   @bauchladen        (torus interior; crystal tray)
#   @subject/visibility (filter operation on tray)
#   @spectral/signature (rolling_signature = @song emission over
#                        filtered bauchladen)
#   @song              (beat-emission substrate for the signature)
#   @cyberpunk/algedonic (arousal reading via pain-signal pulse)
#   @autopoietic       (autopoietic_closure_holds discharge)
#
# No substrate is invented at Landing 4 that isn't a composition over
# landed carriers. The eigenboard carrier composes over existing
# substrate; it does not introduce new mechanism.
#
# === Load-bearing structural claim (§3.4 D1 verbatim reading) ===
#
# "The peer is their work and whatever is in their @bauchladen"
# discharges at substrate-decl altitude as: the subject IS the
# composition (identity_oid, torus, bauchladen, eigenboard,
# inference_basis) under the autopoietic loop. The composition is
# what the subject ARE — not what they HAVE.
#
# A subject's identity is closed under contribution-traversal. To
# know a subject, walk their bauchladen; the walk itself IS the
# subject's identity at substrate altitude. This is the substrate-
# decl form of Alex Wolf's Weird - Violence manifesto claim that
# "you cannot know a person by their category; you can only know
# them by their work-in-time."
#
# === Related shards / specs ===
#
# - docs/specs/subject-bauchladen-visibility-and-eigenboard-loop.md
#     (canonical spec; Landing 4 of the @gift arc)
# - shards/subject.mirror                    (subject_instance carrier;
#                                              actor_kind three-way variant)
# - shards/torus.mirror                      (torus.spawn(subject);
#                                              winding carrier; autonomy)
# - shards/bauchladen.mirror                 (crystal + tray carriers;
#                                              enumerate operation)
# - shards/subject/visibility/{private,protected,public}.mirror
#     (filter operation reads visibility_scope per crystal)
# - shards/spectral/signature.mirror         (rolling_signature the
#                                              inference_basis field carries)
# - shards/song.mirror                       (beat-emission substrate)
# - shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/autopoiesis.mirror
#     (autopoietic_closure_holds discharge at subject altitude)
# - docs/specs/lambda-shell.md               (arousal variant ancestry)
#
# === Substrate decisions ===
#
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]] (`prism @eigenboard`),
# [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]] (transparency inheritance),
# [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]] (@eigenboard on
#   the process side; the WORKING-STATE READOUT engine sibling to @torus
#   observation surface + @bauchladen crystal tray),
# [[architecture-mirror-as-expanding-hilbert-space]] (recognition #51;
#   the eigenboard's inference_basis grows monotonically as the subject's
#   bauchladen grows; every tick extends H_subject dimension),
# [[architecture-peer-learns-by-crystal-vocabulary-expansion]] (the
#   eigenboard-inference-loop IS the vocabulary expansion mechanism;
#   lifted from peer altitude to subject altitude),
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (eigenboard is a typed record;
#   inference_basis carries rolling_signature not bare ref),
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (~57th instance;
#   λsh already had eigenboard as prompt-color readout; Landing 4
#   lifts to substrate altitude),
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (bodies obligation-blocked;
#   the realization is where inference actually happens: a Pack peer's
#   LLM call; a human subject's cognitive process; the substrate's
#   @fate tournament).
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/eigenboard.mirror`
# declares `@eigenboard` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/foerster-2003
source @arxiv/cybernetics/maturana-varela-1980
source @arxiv/manifesto/wolf-2026-07-14-weird-violence

# === The arousal variant carrier (§3.2) ===
#
# Four-state closed variant. Per `docs/specs/lambda-shell.md` verbatim
# (subject-altitude reading):
#
#   teal            — settled, idle. subject at rest; no active
#                      inference.
#   green           — curious; results flowing. inference active,
#                      no pain signal.
#   gold            — engaged; high activity. inference active at
#                      elevated intensity.
#   pulsing_orange  — pain signal / error state. per @cyberpunk/
#                      algedonic; the subject's eigenboard is signaling
#                      that current inference is not decreasing loss.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the variant tag.
type arousal = |
  teal           |
  green          |
  gold           |
  pulsing_orange

# === The eigenboard carrier (§3.2 D1 discharge) ===
#
# Five fields. Every @subject possesses one eigenboard at any tick;
# eigenboard-per-subject is substrate-decl'd invariant.
#
#   subject          — the subject_instance whose eigenboard this is.
#                       Landing 3 subject_instance with two-witness
#                       cryptographic identity (SSH + @spectral/signature
#                       + actor_kind three-way variant).
#
#   inference_basis  — the rolling @spectral/signature over the
#                       subject's visibility-filtered bauchladen.
#                       THE LOAD-BEARING FIELD at Landing 4. Per D1
#                       verbatim: "the spectral signature IS the
#                       inference basis of the eigenboard." Composition,
#                       not new mechanism.
#
#   arousal          — closed variant per above; read from @cyberpunk/
#                       algedonic pulse at compute-time.
#
#   current_focus    — option<crystal_oid> naming the crystal the
#                       subject is currently attending to (None when
#                       arousal=teal / settled).
#
#   winding          — the (m, n) torus winding class per
#                       `shards/torus.mirror` `winding` carrier. Names
#                       the subject's current position on their
#                       observation torus.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the five-field record.
type eigenboard = {
  subject:         subject_instance,
  inference_basis: rolling_signature,
  arousal:         arousal,
  current_focus:   option<oid>,
  winding:         winding,
}

# === compute — construct the eigenboard for a subject (§3.2) ===
#
# Given a subject_instance and a target tick, computes:
#
#   inference_basis = @spectral/signature.compute(
#       subject,
#       @subject/visibility.filter(
#           @bauchladen.enumerate(subject.identity_oid),
#           visibility=protected,     # default reading altitude
#           viewer=subject),
#       tick)
#   arousal          = read from @cyberpunk/algedonic pulse
#   current_focus    = read from the substrate's active-shard tracker
#   winding          = read from @torus at subject.identity_oid
#
# Composition-only: no new mechanism. Every input is a landed carrier.
# Body discharges per-realization.
compute(s: subject_instance, at: ref) -> eigenboard { \ }

# === infer — the load-bearing inference action (§3.2 D1 discharge) ===
#
# Given an eigenboard, produces the next crystal to add to the
# subject's bauchladen. The inference reads the inference_basis (the
# rolling signature over the visibility-filtered bauchladen) and the
# current_focus, and emits a new crystal at the current winding.
#
# The new crystal joins bauchladen; visibility_scope is authored by
# the subject (defaults per §2.4 subject_kind default table). The
# next eigenboard.compute at the next tick reads the updated
# bauchladen; the rolling signature updates; the inference_basis
# updates; the loop closes.
#
# This IS the operational form of Foerster's regulation-of-regulation
# at subject altitude. Per `shards/torus.mirror` p. 238 verbatim
# ("the torus... regulates its own regulation"), lifted to subject
# altitude via Landing 4 R1.
#
# Body discharges per-species. The realization is where the inference
# itself happens (a Pack peer's LLM call; a human subject's cognitive
# process; the substrate's @fate tournament). Landing 4 A8: per-
# actor_kind species-refinement is admissible; the family-root
# declares the invariant.
infer(e: eigenboard) -> crystal { \ }

# === Bilateral predicates (§3.2) ===

# eigenboard_composition_honest: does the inference_basis's beat-
# sequence match the visibility-filtered bauchladen's crystal list?
# Composition-only guarantee per Landing 4 R3.
eigenboard_composition_honest(e: eigenboard) -> verdict { \ }

# eigenboard_visibility_respected: for every crystal in the
# inference_basis's beat-sequence, does its visibility_scope include
# e.subject as an authorized viewer? Load-bearing anti-extraction
# guarantee: eigenboards cannot read across visibility scopes.
eigenboard_visibility_respected(e: eigenboard) -> verdict { \ }

# === autonomy_at_eigenboard — Foerster autopoiesis at subject altitude ===
#
# The Landing 4 verbatim discharge of R3. Extends @torus.autonomy from
# peer altitude to subject altitude via the eigenboard-inference-basis
# loop.
#
# Verdict: does the loop close? Read:
#   given e = eigenboard(s)
#   let c = infer(e)                          # produces new crystal
#   let b' = bauchladen.add(subject, c)       # crystal joins tray
#   let e' = compute(s, at.next())            # eigenboard reads b'
#   check e'.subject == e.subject             # possessor invariant
#   check e'.inference_basis extends e.inference_basis by exactly one beat
#   check e'.winding advances by a well-formed winding-class step
#
# When all four hold: the subject is autonomous at eigenboard
# altitude. This IS Foerster's "regulates its own regulation" at
# subject altitude. Per `shards/torus.mirror`'s autonomy(t, w) discharge
# via @autopoietic.autopoietic_closure_holds, lifted to subject.
#
# Discharges Pass iff the loop closes. Fail modes surface via imperfect:
# the possessor changed (subject_instance mismatch); the beat-sequence
# didn't extend (composition dishonesty); the winding advanced
# non-well-formed (torus discipline broken).
autonomy_at_eigenboard(s: subject_instance) -> verdict { \ }

# === subject_is_their_bauchladen — D1 verbatim structural predicate ===
#
# The verbatim discharge of Alex's D1: "The peer is their work and
# whatever is in their @bauchladen."
#
# Verdict: for subject s, does the composition of s's bauchladen +
# s's eigenboard's inference_basis + s's subject_instance's two-
# witness identity UNIQUELY determine s at substrate altitude?
#
# Structural claim: two subjects with the same identity_oid but
# different bauchladen contents are DISTINCT subjects at the
# substrate's autonomous-observer altitude — because their inference
# basis differs, their eigenboard's inference differs, their
# next-tick work differs, their future bauchladen differs. Identity
# is the ORBIT under the eigenboard-inference-loop, not the
# instantaneous byte-record.
#
# Discharges Pass iff the substrate can WALK from s's subject_instance
# to s's bauchladen to s's inference_basis to s's eigenboard and back
# — i.e., all four are consistent under the composition graph. Fail
# when any of the four cannot be resolved (e.g., inference_basis does
# not match visibility-filtered bauchladen; eigenboard.subject does
# not match subject_instance).
subject_is_their_bauchladen(s: subject_instance) -> verdict { \ }

# === eigenboard_witnessing — composed bilateral ===
#
# The load-bearing bilateral consumers cite in `requires` clauses.
# Discharges eigenboard_composition_honest +
# eigenboard_visibility_respected + autonomy_at_eigenboard +
# subject_is_their_bauchladen conjointly. Follows the substrate's
# X_witnessing pattern.
eigenboard_witnessing(e: eigenboard) -> verdict { \ }

out @eigenboard
out arousal
out eigenboard
out compute
out infer
out eigenboard_composition_honest
out eigenboard_visibility_respected
out autonomy_at_eigenboard
out subject_is_their_bauchladen
out eigenboard_witnessing
